            "review_title": "Review at David Pizzeria",
            "review_text": "RonTang\nSingapore, Singapore534 contributions\n0\nNot Quite Italian\nDec 2025 • Solo\nI visited this establishment craving for some wholesome Italian pasta. Those who know how good Italian pasta is will be disappointed dining here. Maybe this place is known better for its pizzas, something I did not order as I was alone. My main was a Vongole spaghetti with clams. When my order was served, I was surprised to see that it was tomato based instead of white wine sauce. Thankfully, it wasn’t too tomato-ey. For a coastal town like Vung Tau, one would expect seafood to be good. To my disappointment, the clams were small and not fresh. They were also overcooked. Would I return to this place? I might, just to give their pizzas a taste. There is seating on the ground floor and on the second floor. Although situated across the street from the coast, sea view is somewhat obstructed.\nRead more\nWritten December 18, 2025",
